    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to present 211 Clonliffe Road, Drumcondra, to the market.\n\nThis handsome red-brick period property offers a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial home in a well-established and highly sought-after location. Currently arranged as three separate residential units, the property provides excellent flexibility and, subject to the necessary works and permissions, offers the discerning purchaser the opportunity to reconfigure the accommodation and create a wonderful family home.\n\nThe property is approached via a front garden enclosed by traditional railings, with low hedging to the right, and benefits from attractive bay windows and a distinctive period façade. To the rear is a private garden, with an electronic shutter providing access to the rear laneway.\n\nInternally, the accommodation is currently arranged over three units, all accessed from the main entrance hall. The existing layout provides a useful indication of the property's generous proportions and offers considerable scope for reconfiguration.\n\nThe ground-floor unit comprises a kitchen/living area with an original feature fireplace, a separate bedroom with its own feature fireplace, and a bathroom with shower, WC and wash hand basin. The bedroom also enjoys access to the rear garden.\n\nThe second unit comprises a living room with double doors opening onto the rear garden, a kitchen, bathroom and separate double bedroom overlooking the garden.\n\nThe upper accommodation comprises two double bedrooms, one of which features a period fireplace, a bathroom on the return, a generous living room with kitchen area centred around a feature fireplace, attractive bay windows overlooking the front garden, and a further single room overlooking the front.\n\nThe property retains a number of attractive period features and, with its generous room proportions, front and rear gardens and excellent flexibility of accommodation, presents an exciting opportunity to create a superb family residence. The existing configuration also provides flexibility for those seeking a property with income potential, while the principal appeal lies in the opportunity to restore and reimagine this fine period house as a substantial family home.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the full potential of this impressive property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nUNIT ONE - \n\n\nLiving Room /Kitchen - 4.46m max x 4.01m\nA combined living and kitchen space positioned at the front of the property. The room has a feature fireplace and bay window overlooking the front garden, with the kitchen area located to one side.\n\nBedroom One - 3.48m x 3.78m\nA double bedroom positioned with a feature fireplace and access towards the rear garden.\n\nEn-suite - 1.20m x 1.43m\nLocated off the bedroom and fitted with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nUNIT TWO - \n\n\nLiving Room - 4.71m x 2.83m\nA well-proportioned room positioned towards the centre of the property, double doors opening onto the rear garden.\n\nKitchen - 2.37m x 1.78m\nKitchen located towards the rear of the unit.\n\nBathroom - 2.34m x 1.09m\nSeparate bathroom fitted with shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.78m x 2.97m\nA double bedroom located to the rear, with a window overlooking the garden.\n\nUNIT THREE - \n\n\nLiving Room/Kitchen - 4.48m x 3.80m\nCombined living and kitchen room located towards the front of the property. The room incorporates a feature fireplace and bay window overlooking the front garden.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.63m x 3.76m\nA double bedroom located to the rear of the property, with a feature fireplace and outlook over the rear garden.\n\nBedroom Four - 4.00m x 2.89m\nA further double bedroom positioned towards the rear of the property, overlooking the rear garden.\n\nBedroom Five - 3.56m x 1.95m\nA single room located to the front of the property, with a window overlooking the front garden.\n\nBathroom - 1.63m x 1.73\nBathroom located on the return, fitted with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Handsome red-brick period property</li><li> Currently arranged as three separate residential units</li><li> Excellent potential to reconfigure as a substantial family home</li><li> Original and feature fireplaces</li><li> Attractive bay windows</li><li> Front and rear gardens</li><li> Electronic rear shutter with access to laneway</li><li> Excellent potential in a highly sought-after location</li><li> Adjacent Drumcondra Train Station and Village</li><li> Close to Croke Park, the Mater Hospital and Temple Street Childrens Hospital</li><li> 2km North of the GPO, Dublin City Centre</li><li> Easy access to M1/M50 intersection and Dublin Airport</ul>"
      },
